Article 3 (Composition of the Committee)
(1) The Committee shall consist of not more than 13 members, including one Chairperson and one Executive Member.
(2) The Director General of the National Court Administration shall appoint or commission the members from among persons falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Judges;
2. Prosecutors;
3. Attorneys-at-law;
4. Professors of law;
5. Other persons with knowledge and experience.
(3) The Chairperson and the Executive Member shall be designated by the Director General of the National Court Administration from among the Committee members.
(4) The term of office of Committee members shall be two years, and members may be reappointed or recommissioned.
(5) The Director General of the National Court Administration may dismiss or release a member from appointment or commission in any of the following cases:
1. Where the member is deemed unable to perform duties due to an unavoidable reason;
2. Where the member violates a duty arising from the member's office;
3. Where the member is otherwise deemed unfit to retain the qualifications of a Committee member.
